{% block content %}
<section class="page-hero">
    <div class="page-hero-inner">
        <p class="page-eyebrow">Our Story / Why GÜTE</p>
        <h1 class="page-title">We're the ones who<br><em>flip it over.</em></h1>
        <p class="page-lead">Hard to pronounce ingredients. No time to look them up at the aisle. We felt that — and we also happened to know exactly what those ingredients were.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-seal" role="img" aria-label="GÜTE seal — good for your gut, good for our planet"></div>
</section>

<div class="content-wrap">
    <div class="problem-block reveal">
        <p class="section-stamp">The Problem</p>
        <div class="prose">
            <p>You're at the shopping aisle. You're craving something. You pick up a bar, flip it over — and the ingredient list is a paragraph of things you can't pronounce. Who has time to look all that up while you're just trying to grab a snack?</p>
            <p>We know that feeling. Except we also spent <strong>20 years working in food</strong> — reading labels, tracing supply chains, writing food safety plans. We know what those ingredients are. We know why they're in there. And a lot of the time, the answer isn't a good one.</p>
            <p>That's the thing about being a food safety professional. You stop being able to eat without thinking about it. We found ourselves turning over our favorite snacks and not loving what we found — and eventually deciding to do something about it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pull-line">We wanted to make a product <em>for people like us.</em><br>The ones who flip it over.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="founders-block reveal">
        <p class="section-stamp">Who We Are</p>
        <div class="prose"><p>We're Li and Benson — two health-conscious foodies with a combined 20 years in the food industry, a shared obsession with what's actually in our food, and apparently the same idea at the same time.</p></div>
        <div class="founders-grid">
            <div class="founder-card">
                <div class="founder-initial">L</div>
                <h3 class="founder-name">Li</h3>
                <p class="founder-role">Co-Founder</p>
                <div class="founder-certs"><span class="cert">SQF Practitioner</span><span class="cert">HACCP Certified</span><span class="cert">PCQI</span><span class="cert">FSVP</span><span class="cert">ASQ CMQ-OE</span></div>
                <p class="founder-bio">Background in nutrition science, food science, and food safety. The combination that lets you see both sides of a label — what it says, and what it means. Passionate about food that's genuinely good for you, not just marketed that way.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="founder-card">
                <div class="founder-initial">B</div>
                <h3 class="founder-name">Benson</h3>
                <p class="founder-role">Co-Founder</p>
                <div class="founder-certs"><span class="cert">SQF Practitioner</span><span class="cert">HACCP Certified</span><span class="cert">PCQI</span><span class="cert">FSVP</span><span class="cert">ServSafe Manager</span></div>
                <p class="founder-bio">Studied environmental science, stumbled into food safety, and never left. The systems thinking that comes from environmental work maps perfectly onto food — traceability, upstream impact, what's actually in things and where it came from. It's also why sustainability isn't an afterthought at GÜTE — from plant-based sourcing to recyclable paper packaging, lower impact is a design requirement, not a marketing line.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="experience-bar">
            <div class="exp-num">20</div>
            <div><p class="exp-label">Combined years in food</p><p class="exp-desc">Enough time to know what's worth eating — and what we'd rather build ourselves.</p></div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="name-block reveal">
        <p class="section-stamp">Why GÜTE</p>
        <div class="prose"><p>We wanted a name that meant something. Not a made-up word or a lifestyle-coded acronym — something that actually said what we were trying to do.</p></div>
        <div class="name-grid">
            <div class="name-card dark">
                <div class="name-word">Güte</div>
                <p class="name-sub">German — "Good"</p>
                <p class="name-desc">Good ingredients. Good process. Good for you. Good for the planet. One word that covers the whole thing — and signals quality without having to explain itself.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="name-card light">
                <div class="name-word"><em>Gut</em>e</div>
                <p class="name-sub">The function — Gut Health</p>
                <p class="name-desc">Gut is right there in the name. That wasn't an accident. Our product is designed from the core up to be good for your gut — real fiber, real ingredients, nothing your body has to fight through to get to the good stuff.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="verbatim">
            <blockquote>"Dietary fiber feeds your microbiome and helps keep things moving on the regular, but most of us aren't getting nearly enough of this unsung nutrient."</blockquote>
            <cite>— <a href="https://med.stanford.edu/news/insights/2026/06/fiber-facts-science-how-much-do-you-need.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Stanford Medicine</a></cite>
        </div>
        <p class="verbatim-follow">That's the gap we set out to close. <strong>We wanted to build something that tastes good while nourishing your gut</strong> — delivering an essential nutrient as an indulgent experience, not a medicinal one. Fiber in a form you'll actually reach for.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="product-block reveal">
        <p class="section-stamp">What We Built</p>
        <div class="prose">
            <p>GÜTE Crunch is where we started. A functional snack bar built on an ancient grain and plant protein core, dusted in whole blueberry powder, finished in dark chocolate. Every ingredient is there because it earns its spot — not because it's cheap, not to hit a number on the label, and not because a flavor house recommended it.</p>
            <p>We're a small-batch, artisanal operation. That's not a constraint we're working around — it's how we keep the standard honest while we're getting started.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="good-grid">
            <div class="good-cell" style="background-image: linear-gradient(rgba(250,245,236,0.58), rgba(250,245,236,0.72)), url('/images/Panel/good-ingredients.png'); background-size: cover; background-position: center;"><div class="good-word">Good <em>ingredients.</em></div><p class="good-detail">Seven ancient grains &amp; seeds, dual plant-based protein, five dietary fibers. Every one verified by two people who read labels for a living.</p></div>
            <div class="good-cell" style="background-image: linear-gradient(rgba(250,245,236,0.58), rgba(250,245,236,0.72)), url('/images/Panel/good-gut.png'); background-size: cover; background-position: center;"><div class="good-word">Good for <em>your gut.</em></div><p class="good-detail">Natural fiber from fruits, grains &amp; seeds — plus green banana flour, cassava fiber, acacia fiber, oat bran fiber, and psyllium husk. A fiber stack that actually does something.</p></div>
            <div class="good-cell" style="background-image: linear-gradient(rgba(250,245,236,0.58), rgba(250,245,236,0.72)), url('/images/Panel/plant-protein.png'); background-size: cover; background-position: center;"><div class="good-word">Plant-based <em>protein.</em></div><p class="good-detail">Pea and rice protein together — a more complete amino acid profile than either alone. No dairy, no whey, no isolate shortcuts.</p></div>
            <div class="good-cell" style="background-image: linear-gradient(rgba(250,245,236,0.58), rgba(250,245,236,0.72)), url('/images/Panel/freeze-dried-fruit.png'); background-size: cover; background-position: center;"><div class="good-word">Freeze-dried <em>fruit.</em></div><p class="good-detail">Whole lemon, blueberry, and cranberry — freeze-dried to a powder and dusted on before enrobing. Real fruit, not flavoring.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="bridge">
            <div class="bridge-text">
                <p class="bridge-label">Want to see exactly what's in it?</p>
                <p class="bridge-headline">Five FDA-recognized fibers.<br><em>All of them explained.</em></p>
            </div>
            <a href="/ingredients.html" class="bridge-link">See the Ingredients →</a>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="cause-block reveal">
        <p class="section-stamp">For a Good Cause / Sustainability</p>
        <div class="prose">
            <p>"Good for the planet" isn't a line we bolt on at the end — it's built into how we make GÜTE. We keep batches <strong>small and hand-stamped</strong>: less waste, tighter quality control, and no giant runs sitting in a warehouse. Every bar is plant-based, so its footprint starts lower than anything built on dairy or animal protein.</p>
            <p>Our packaging is <strong>paper-based and recyclable</strong> — no mixed-material film that can't be recycled, no plastic clamshells. It's the same rule we apply to the ingredient list: if it doesn't earn its place, it doesn't go in.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pull-line">Good ingredients, good process, <em>good for the planet.</em></div>
    </div>

    <div class="story-cta reveal">
        <p class="cta-eyebrow">Reserve / First Batch</p>
        <h2 class="cta-title">You've read the story.<br><em>Try the bar.</em></h2>
        <a href="/#reserve" class="cta-btn">Join the Waitlist →</a>
    </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
